      "text": "To solve the given problem, we need to compute the sum of the floor values of the square roots of integers from 1 to 16. The floor function $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ returns the greatest integer less than or equal to $x$. Thus, we need to find $\\lfloor \\sqrt{1} \\rfloor, \\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor, \\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor, \\ldots, \\lfloor \\sqrt{16} \\rfloor$ and then sum these values. We can compute $\\lfloor \\sqrt{k} \\rfloor$ for each integer $k$ from 1 to 16 and sum the results.\n\nLet's write the Python code to do this.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the sum of floor(sqrt(k)) for k from 1 to 16\ntotal_sum = sum(math.floor(math.sqrt(k)) for k in range(1, 17))\n\nprint(total_sum)\n```\n```output\n43\n```\nThe sum of the floor values of the square roots from 1 to 16 is \\(\\boxed{43}\\).",
